{"name":"Vantablack","hex":"#000100","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Vantablack","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A class of super-black coatings that absorb almost all light.","An exceedingly dark shade of black."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or relating to a very dark shade of black; Vantablack."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Vantablack"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vantablack","blocks":[{"text":"Vantablack is a class of super-black coatings with total hemispherical reflectances (THR) below 1% in the visible spectrum. The name is a compound of the acronym VANTA and black."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Vantablack_02.JPG/330px-Vantablack_02.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vantablack","wikidata":"Q17394326"},{"title":"Vantablack (EP)","blocks":[{"text":"Vantablack is a collaborative extended play by French electronic band Dirtyphonics and Los Angeles–based electronic rock producer Sullivan King. Vantablack was released on 3 November 2017, by the independent electronic music label, Monstercat. The EP features six songs, all of which were produced by both producers."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2c/Vantablack_EP.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vantablack_(EP)","wikidata":"Q42888106"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Vantablack_01.JPG/500px-Vantablack_01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Vantablack_01.JPG/1280px-Vantablack_01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Vantablack_01.JPG/500px-Vantablack_01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_